      "type": "text",
      "text": "No. The attribution says only that the model relied on features near the basic amine when producing its **hERG prediction**. It does not show that the amine binds a particular residue, enters the pore, or causes block.\n\nAt most, it supports a mechanistic hypothesis: the protonated amine may contribute to electrostatic interactions in the hERG inner cavity, consistent with known hERG blocker behavior. That hypothesis needs independent evidence such as:\n\n- hERG mutagenesis, especially pore-residue substitutions\n- Patch-clamp measurements of state/use dependence and kinetics\n- pH or ionization dependence\n- Analog comparisons that selectively alter the amine\n\nAlso check the attribution\u2019s `explainer_validation`: even if it performs better than a random control, it remains a model signal, not mechanistic evidence.",
